WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.500
{ED}

00:00:01.430 --> 00:00:04.170
Oh beautiful Osaka...{Naniwa is an old name for Osaka. I feel that'd be a step too far in the cultural preservation stakes, however, but let's ensure it stays as Osaka at the very least and doesn't end up translated as "Who is that beautiful girl Kamen." Yes, this is a thing that has happened in a sub when Naniwa came up. It's not pretty.}{TLC: o_O how did that happen?}

00:00:04.270 --> 00:00:05.810
Heave, ho...

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:12.320
D-Darling...

00:00:12.520 --> 00:00:14.050
Akane...

00:00:14.660 --> 00:00:17.020
Dad?! Oh, Go-

00:00:18.990 --> 00:00:21.960
Guess I'm gonna be stuck here for a while, huh?

00:00:21.960 --> 00:00:23.680
What a shock!

00:00:23.680 --> 00:00:25.190
Slipped disk, huh?

00:00:25.190 --> 00:00:27.620
Yeah! You had me freaking out!

00:00:27.620 --> 00:00:28.700
Ow!

00:00:28.700 --> 00:00:29.800
Laughing just makes it hurt...

00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:31.770
So, what're we gonna do about the shop?

00:00:32.120 --> 00:00:36.520
Good point... making okonomiyaki's never been my strong point.

00:00:36.520 --> 00:00:38.560
Guess we'll have to close up for a while.{TLC: better make it clear he means temporarily by adding "until I'm better" "for a while" or something}

00:00:38.560 --> 00:00:41.250
What about the neighborhood meeting though?{But what about the neighborhood meeting?}{TLC: (literally "the eating-together-thing on the weekend") sug. "But what about Sunday's booking?"}

00:00:41.430 --> 00:00:43.550
Isn't the chief of the neighborhood association coming?{TLC: would need to make this "neighborhood association" for context if the above line is changed}

00:00:43.940 --> 00:00:46.370
Oh, right, he is, isn't he...

00:00:48.520 --> 00:00:51.990
Well, there's no point closing up if I can run the place!

00:00:53.300 --> 00:00:54.400
No?

00:00:54.660 --> 00:00:57.340
Why not? You're a pretty good chef, Akane!

00:00:57.340 --> 00:00:59.700
I agree. Wanna give it a shot?

00:00:59.700 --> 00:01:05.970
Alright! Time for me to save us from the brink of peril!

00:01:08.920 --> 00:01:10.480
Smile! Smile! Smile! Smile!

00:01:10.480 --> 00:01:12.320
Smile Precure!

00:01:12.620 --> 00:01:13.220
Let's go!

00:01:13.220 --> 00:01:14.760
Smile! Smile! Precure!

00:01:14.760 --> 00:01:15.890
All together!

00:01:16.120 --> 00:01:17.490
Smile! Smile! Precure!

00:01:17.490 --> 00:01:19.690
Jump to tomorrow!

00:01:19.860 --> 00:01:22.360
Smile Precure!

00:01:24.230 --> 00:01:27.200
Smile! Smile! Smile Precure!

00:01:27.470 --> 00:01:32.640
A smile, shining like the sun.

00:01:33.010 --> 00:01:37.850
We all carry an undying sparkle.

00:01:38.580 --> 00:01:43.780
Keep going with all you've got, girls!

00:01:44.150 --> 00:01:48.720
Those beads of sweat are diamonds.

00:01:48.120 --> 00:01:48.690
So bright!

00:01:48.720 --> 00:01:53.890
The future that you'll shine the way to

00:01:54.260 --> 00:02:00.330
When five lights seize the will to win.

00:01:58.300 --> 00:02:00.840
Happy! Sunny! Peace! March! Beauty!

00:02:01.370 --> 00:02:02.000
Let's go!

00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:04.710
(Smile! Smile!) The power of a smile

00:02:04.710 --> 00:02:07.640
(Smile! Smile!) Joins us all together.

00:02:07.980 --> 00:02:12.450
We'll never let a friend cry!

00:02:11.810 --> 00:02:13.010
Girls! Let's go!

00:02:13.080 --> 00:02:14.680
Smile! Smile! Precure!

00:02:14.680 --> 00:02:15.820
Everybody!

00:02:15.850 --> 00:02:17.490
Smile! Smile! Precure!

00:02:17.490 --> 00:02:20.020
Fly to the future!

00:02:20.350 --> 00:02:23.520
Sparkle! Smile Precure!

00:02:24.290 --> 00:02:25.690
Smile! Smile! Smile! Smile!

00:02:25.690 --> 00:02:28.000
Smile Precure!

00:02:37.100 --> 00:02:40.930
I'm not gonna be up to doing anything until I get a good meal...

00:02:44.120 --> 00:02:45.280
What're you making?

00:02:45.280 --> 00:02:47.330
My latest potion-da wasa!

00:02:47.330 --> 00:02:48.180
Is it tasty?

00:02:48.420 --> 00:02:53.010
It's made of lizard tails, pig drool and frog farts!

00:02:53.010 --> 00:02:54.010
I'll... take that as a no...

00:02:54.740 --> 00:02:57.470
Perhaps this'll be more to your taste, then-da wasa?

00:02:58.510 --> 00:03:01.990
What's this? Okonomiyaki?

00:03:04.010 --> 00:03:06.560
Savory pancakes, huh... yeah, I can go for some of those!{I'm rewriting this line to explain what an okonomiyaki is to our Western audience, as I don't think we've (or at least I've?) actually explained what one is in-show thusfar.}

00:03:06.560 --> 00:03:08.090
Then it's settled!

00:03:09.300 --> 00:03:14.270
I'll go to the humans' world, get some grub, and take out those Precure! Two birds with one stone!

00:03:14.290 --> 00:03:19.440
I am such a genius!

00:03:27.650 --> 00:03:28.650
A-Akane's...

00:03:28.650 --> 00:03:29.620
running...

00:03:29.620 --> 00:03:31.090
the shop?!

00:03:32.550 --> 00:03:37.890
Hey, I wouldn't say runnin'. Just, you know, fillin' in for my dad until he gets better.

00:03:37.890 --> 00:03:40.500
I'm impressed, Akane-chan!

00:03:40.500 --> 00:03:42.470
That's amazing, Akane-chan!

00:03:42.840 --> 00:03:45.870
Well, I wouldn't go that far... but if you insist!

00:03:45.870 --> 00:03:49.160
I don't think modesty works that way, you know.

00:03:51.150 --> 00:03:54.460
Really though, the biggest problem's gonna be Sunday.

00:03:54.460 --> 00:03:55.580
Why's that?

00:03:55.910 --> 00:04:00.580
The chief of the neighborhood association is bringing everyone to our place for a dinner.

00:04:00.580 --> 00:04:05.290
{I'm assuming this isn't Akane.}Ah, yes. I'd heard he was rather a connoisseur when it came to fine dining.

00:04:05.290 --> 00:04:06.540
C-Connowhat?

00:04:06.540 --> 00:04:08.200
A gourmet.

00:04:08.200 --> 00:04:09.120
Oh!

00:04:09.120 --> 00:04:10.110
You got it!

00:04:10.110 --> 00:04:14.040
So, this guy, the gourmet association chief, really likes my dad's okonomiyaki.

00:04:14.040 --> 00:04:18.790
"The finest okonomiyaki I've ever eaten in my entire life", he said.

00:04:18.790 --> 00:04:21.340
I've gotta live up to my dad's reputation and serve up a 5-star feast!

00:04:21.340 --> 00:04:25.530
Your okonomiyaki must be absolutely out of this world, then!

00:04:25.530 --> 00:04:30.790
My mom says that it's miles better than anything she could make at home!

00:04:31.530 --> 00:04:33.790
I'm getting hungry just talking about it...

00:04:33.790 --> 00:04:35.420
I wanna try some-kuru!

00:04:39.020 --> 00:04:43.990
Alright then! After you get home from school, come round to my place for a feast!

00:04:43.990 --> 00:04:45.890
Alright!

00:04:50.810 --> 00:04:52.230
Is it done yet?

00:04:52.230 --> 00:04:53.800
It does require cooking, you know.

00:04:53.800 --> 00:04:55.970
Ain't no rushing perfection!

00:04:56.220 --> 00:04:57.310
Akane-san...

00:04:57.310 --> 00:04:57.940
Yeah?

00:04:57.940 --> 00:05:01.410
Is your family's restaurant named...?

00:05:01.410 --> 00:05:02.340
Yeah...

00:05:02.340 --> 00:05:04.450
They named it after me.

00:05:04.450 --> 00:05:11.490
They opened it up the year I was born, and wanted it to be as special to 'em as I was.

00:05:11.490 --> 00:05:13.790
What a lovely sentiment.

00:05:14.940 --> 00:05:16.590
I can't wait anymore!

00:05:16.880 --> 00:05:19.330
Cookin' these things ain't that simple, ya know! Watch!

00:05:19.330 --> 00:05:22.860
A one, a two, a one, two, three...

00:05:31.980 --> 00:05:35.880
Behold, the Hino family's most venerable technique! The Scoop-Flip Special!

00:05:35.880 --> 00:05:38.910
See, I know my okonomiyaki!

00:05:40.610 --> 00:05:42.190
It's lovely...

00:05:42.190 --> 00:05:43.920
This is delicious, Akane!

00:05:43.920 --> 00:05:45.460
See, told you!

00:05:45.460 --> 00:05:49.150
Our very own unmatchable Osakan-style okonomiyaki! {Well for one unimitable is apparently inimitable, and 2 that doesn't sound like Akane at all}

00:05:49.150 --> 00:05:50.420
I'm home!

00:05:50.590 --> 00:05:51.850
Genki!

00:05:52.810 --> 00:05:54.420
What?

00:05:54.420 --> 00:05:55.820
This is my brother, Genki.

00:05:55.820 --> 00:05:56.920
Hey.

00:05:56.920 --> 00:05:58.870
Introduce yourself properly!

00:06:00.270 --> 00:06:04.200
I'm sorry 'bout my crazy sister. I bet she storms you off into all sorts of trouble, doesn't she? {Is this second sentence supposed to not make sense?}

00:06:04.660 --> 00:06:06.260
What was that?!

00:06:06.260 --> 00:06:07.500
Well, am I wrong?

00:06:07.500 --> 00:06:11.610
Oh hey, you cooked this up? Don't mind if I help myself~!

00:06:11.610 --> 00:06:12.910
Hey, mind your manners!

00:06:14.440 --> 00:06:16.160
Hey, that's not bad.

00:06:16.160 --> 00:06:18.290
Not quite like Dad's, but nice.

00:06:18.510 --> 00:06:19.050
Huh?!

00:06:19.050 --> 00:06:22.770
Guess it's more your style, though. Thanks for the food, anyway!

00:06:23.860 --> 00:06:26.110
That made me so <i>ultra happy</i>!

00:06:26.110 --> 00:06:27.060
Oh crap...

00:06:27.060 --> 00:06:28.530
What? What's wrong?

00:06:28.830 --> 00:06:30.830
None of these are good...{I can't serve 'em this!}{TLC: "They're all terrible!" okay, Ed, please find a better phrasing, but the point is that she's making so many, and they're all turning out no good}{RL: I'm just going with that since I have no clue which of us on the staff is named Ed so I have no clue who you're talking to...}

00:06:30.830 --> 00:06:35.140
That chief guy's been lookin' forward to my dad's cooking!

00:06:35.140 --> 00:06:37.600
He won't be satisfied with anything less.

00:06:39.570 --> 00:06:41.780
What am I doin' wrong?!

00:06:41.780 --> 00:06:45.790
I'm usin' the same ingredients, followin' the same recipe...

00:06:45.790 --> 00:06:50.610
Ah, hey! I think Dad said he had some kinda secret ingredient!

00:06:50.610 --> 00:06:52.120
A secret ingredient?!

00:06:52.380 --> 00:06:54.430
Well, what is it?

00:06:54.430 --> 00:06:55.590
Well, it's...

00:06:57.100 --> 00:06:58.090
Actually, I dunno!

00:07:00.590 --> 00:07:02.150
A secret ingredient...

00:07:02.150 --> 00:07:05.960
If I knew what it was, I could make it like he does...

00:07:07.550 --> 00:07:09.140
Alright... I'll just have to figure it out!

00:07:09.540 --> 00:07:12.340
Time to try to recreate my dad's recipe!{TLC: sug. "try and make"->"recreate"}

00:07:12.340 --> 00:07:13.790
I'll help too!

00:07:13.790 --> 00:07:14.770
Me too!

00:07:14.770 --> 00:07:15.610
I shall as well.

00:07:15.610 --> 00:07:16.540
That's the spirit!

00:07:16.910 --> 00:07:18.380
You'll help...?

00:07:18.920 --> 00:07:20.250
Thanks so much!

00:07:24.220 --> 00:07:26.690
These are the ingredients we normally use.

00:07:26.690 --> 00:07:30.090
What could the secret ingredient be?

00:07:30.090 --> 00:07:32.660
Perhaps it is a case of sugar and spice.

00:07:32.660 --> 00:07:34.030
Sugar and spice...?

00:07:34.030 --> 00:07:34.860
Indeed.

00:07:34.860 --> 00:07:37.040
Something sweet to complement something spicy.

00:07:37.040 --> 00:07:38.970
Something spicy to complement something sweet.

00:07:38.970 --> 00:07:42.400
My grandfather always taught me this was a fundamental way of drawing out flavor.

00:07:42.400 --> 00:07:45.340
That's true. We always use grated apples when we make curry.

00:07:45.340 --> 00:07:48.040
Huh, that's an interesting idea. So like, some kinda seasoning...

00:07:48.040 --> 00:07:49.880
Something sweet to complement something spicy.

00:07:49.880 --> 00:07:51.640
Something spicy to complement something sweet.

00:07:51.640 --> 00:07:53.280
The sauce she uses is spicy!

00:07:53.280 --> 00:07:54.250
Then ta-da!

00:07:55.310 --> 00:07:56.480
How about sesame oil?{help I can't work out what she's saying over the fucking LET'S GO PUDDING}?{TLC: sesame oil (ごま油)}

00:07:55.380 --> 00:07:57.870
Let's Go: Pudding!{YOU COOK A DEAD GUY GIGA PUDDING}

00:07:56.480 --> 00:07:59.680
It'll give it a really alluring smell, and draw out the flavor.

00:08:01.360 --> 00:08:02.680
What the heck are you doin?!

00:08:02.680 --> 00:08:04.660
And that is how you make crème caramel!

00:08:08.230 --> 00:08:10.730
Alright then!

00:08:11.340 --> 00:08:13.770
Reika, try adding some of that!{TLC: FWIW: "try adding some of that!"}{RL: Someone really needs to tell me WTF "FWIW" is supposed to mean...}

00:08:13.770 --> 00:08:14.660
Very well.

00:08:14.660 --> 00:08:16.820
Nao, be gentle when you stir it, 'kay?

00:08:16.820 --> 00:08:17.870
OK!

00:08:18.130 --> 00:08:19.900
How about some cream?

00:08:19.900 --> 00:08:21.510
Ooh, and oranges!

00:08:21.510 --> 00:08:23.610
Sweet, sweet honey-kuru!

00:08:23.940 --> 00:08:25.700
Let's try 'em all out!

00:08:25.700 --> 00:08:27.470
Okay!

00:08:28.420 --> 00:08:30.620
I'm full...

00:08:36.140 --> 00:08:38.680
Yeah, none of these are it...

00:08:38.680 --> 00:08:42.140
Huh... they were all really good, though!

00:08:42.140 --> 00:08:44.770
I suppose it is a secret ingredient for a reason.

00:08:44.770 --> 00:08:47.970
It's not gonna be that easy to find, huh?

00:08:49.240 --> 00:08:50.520
Akane?

00:08:50.520 --> 00:08:52.940
Ya know... my dad's really something!

00:08:54.880 --> 00:08:57.660
Not somethin' I'd admit to him, but...

00:08:58.200 --> 00:09:02.470
I really look up to him!

00:09:03.220 --> 00:09:06.450
His okonomiyaki is out of this world!

00:09:06.870 --> 00:09:10.920
It puts a smile on the face of anyone who eats it.

00:09:10.920 --> 00:09:14.560
No matter how sad they look, it always seems to work like magic.

00:09:14.560 --> 00:09:15.670
This is good!

00:09:15.670 --> 00:09:17.530
It really surrounds and warms your heart.{It really warms your heart!}{TLC: "warms the cockles of your heart" is the idiom, not that I'm a huge fan of it. as a suggestion: "makes you feel all warm [deep] inside" or something (to Ed: the Japanese is both literal and metaphoric)}

00:09:17.530 --> 00:09:19.050
Alright, that's the stuff! {or "That feels good!"}

00:09:19.050 --> 00:09:23.540
When it comes down to it, I think that's somethin' only my dad can do.

00:09:24.000 --> 00:09:29.380
And here I am thinkin' I can figure out his secret...

00:09:30.550 --> 00:09:31.900
Akane-chan...

00:09:31.900 --> 00:09:34.750
Alright, no more bein' stupid!

00:09:36.090 --> 00:09:38.820
I guess I'll just have to go ask him!

00:09:39.980 --> 00:09:41.890
I'm hungry like the wolf~{DON'T YOU DARE BITCH ABOUT THIS LEANGLE THIS IS GENIUS THAT YOUR INSIGNIFICANTLY TINY PEA BRAIN CANNOT HOPE TO COMPREHEND}{TLC: -_-'}{Editor: If we get complaints about this I'm blaming mag... It's all his fault... I tried to stop him...}

00:09:42.190 --> 00:09:45.610
I'm terribly sorry, sir, but may I please ask you to remove your mask?

00:09:45.610 --> 00:09:46.710
Mask?

00:09:46.710 --> 00:09:49.060
I'm afraid it might scare the other customers.

00:09:49.060 --> 00:09:54.080
You're worried I'll scare them? Scaring is what I do!

00:09:54.080 --> 00:09:55.240
For I, Wolfrun, am...

00:09:55.240 --> 00:09:58.480
Come back when you're prepared to be reasonable!

00:10:00.070 --> 00:10:03.050
What's with them? Now I've got to find somewhere else...{I grace them with my presence, and get that...}{TLC: second part is about [the disappointment after] finding a place to eat at last [after all that searching].  "Now I've got to find somewhere else!"}

00:10:03.050 --> 00:10:06.490
Oh! I smell food!

00:10:06.490 --> 00:10:11.990
Alright! Time to gobble up all these humans' food!

00:10:16.500 --> 00:10:17.870
Sunny!

00:10:23.360 --> 00:10:24.650
Akanbe!

00:10:26.590 --> 00:10:27.980
My secret ingredient?

00:10:27.980 --> 00:10:31.290
I can't get mine to taste anything like yours!

00:10:31.660 --> 00:10:33.380
So come on, please!

00:10:33.380 --> 00:10:36.690
What have I been teachin' you all this time for?

00:10:36.690 --> 00:10:41.030
Look at you, Miss "I can run the shop!"

00:10:41.260 --> 00:10:43.860
Your name doesn't belong on it!

00:10:44.730 --> 00:10:48.040
Fine then!

00:10:48.040 --> 00:10:51.450
I can figure it out by myself!

00:10:51.450 --> 00:10:53.960
You get on that!

00:10:54.700 --> 00:10:58.060
I'll show you what I've learned!

00:11:00.440 --> 00:11:02.050
She's so easy to manipulate...

00:11:02.670 --> 00:11:04.520
You do it, girl...

00:11:06.490 --> 00:11:08.090
No good?

00:11:08.090 --> 00:11:11.600
"You can figure it out for yourself!" is all I got out of him...

00:11:11.600 --> 00:11:14.290
But that dinner's in three days!

00:11:15.180 --> 00:11:18.390
Oh man! There's no turning back now!

00:11:18.390 --> 00:11:21.340
We'll just have to give it everything we've got!{TLC: "give it what we've got" "put on our best show"}

00:12:01.840 --> 00:12:03.780
How're you feeling?

00:12:08.590 --> 00:12:09.510
Akane.

00:12:11.820 --> 00:12:14.120
I wonder...

00:12:14.120 --> 00:12:17.430
Do you remember the first time you made okonomiyaki?

00:12:17.430 --> 00:12:20.920
Yeah... it was when you had a really bad cold.

00:12:26.440 --> 00:12:30.030
"Mom, eat this and you'll feel better!"{TLC: sug. the more literal "Mom, eat this and [you'll] get/feel better!" here 1) it reads more easily, 2) it has better nuance (Akane is her being her usual confident self, not just "I hope") 3) the extra contrast between the definite "eat this to get better" and the burnt okonomiyaki on the plate improves the gag}

00:12:30.030 --> 00:12:33.640
That okonomiyaki was absolutely delicious, you know.

00:12:36.190 --> 00:12:39.340
Seriously?! But it was all burnt!

00:12:39.340 --> 00:12:41.620
How the heck was it even edible?

00:12:41.620 --> 00:12:44.450
True, it was burnt.

00:12:45.000 --> 00:12:48.790
But to your mother, it was the best meal I could have asked for.

00:12:53.330 --> 00:12:59.030
I just wish I could make okonomiyaki that'd make <i>everyone</i> happy, like dad's do...{TLC: sug. emphasising "everyone" ("making Mum happy isn't enough" is the subtext). also "like dad's does"->"like Dad's do"}

00:13:04.290 --> 00:13:05.930
Three with pork, please.

00:13:05.930 --> 00:13:07.010
Coming right up!

00:13:07.250 --> 00:13:09.170
Thanks!

00:13:09.170 --> 00:13:12.270
Huh, I didn't know this event was going on.

00:13:12.270 --> 00:13:17.190
Yup. It's all to drum up business for the shopping district, help build the place up a bit, you know?

00:13:17.190 --> 00:13:20.720
I'm glad you came to help us out though, Genki-kun!

00:13:20.720 --> 00:13:24.150
It means Akane-chan has more time to figure out that secret ingredient!

00:13:25.300 --> 00:13:26.500
Hello?

00:13:26.840 --> 00:13:29.770
I'm gonna bring over some tests I cooked up, so try 'em and lemme know what you think!

00:13:29.770 --> 00:13:31.230
Roger that!

00:13:31.870 --> 00:13:33.260
Sis and the others are popping round to the stall in a bit.

00:13:33.260 --> 00:13:33.870
Really?

00:13:35.570 --> 00:13:38.540
I haven't eaten in three whole days...

00:13:41.910 --> 00:13:43.480
Wow!

00:13:45.080 --> 00:13:47.750
That's gotta be it! Okonomiyaki!

00:13:47.750 --> 00:13:51.120
Oh, I'm gonna gobble you up, and nothing's gonna stop me!

00:13:51.710 --> 00:13:55.230
This world will be stained with the worst possible conclusion...

00:13:55.230 --> 00:13:57.690
...a Bad End!

00:13:57.690 --> 00:14:01.700
The blank slate of your future will be clouded in darkness!

00:14:06.650 --> 00:14:08.400
I'm not hungry anymore...

00:14:08.400 --> 00:14:10.040
I don't wanna eat anything...

00:14:10.040 --> 00:14:11.910
Okonomiyaki's yucky, anyway...

00:14:13.880 --> 00:14:21.890
The Bad Energy we gather from the humans will resurrect the Emperor of Darkness, King Pierrot-sama!

00:14:26.460 --> 00:14:30.660
I'll be taking their Bad Energy, and your okonomiyaki!

00:14:30.660 --> 00:14:31.460
It's him...!

00:14:31.460 --> 00:14:32.760
It's Wolfrun-kuru!

00:14:32.760 --> 00:14:34.830
Quickly, transform-kuru!

00:14:38.540 --> 00:14:39.810
Ready?

00:14:40.340 --> 00:14:43.220
Precure, Smile Charge!

00:14:43.220 --> 00:14:44.330
Go!

00:14:45.280 --> 00:14:46.590
Go, go!

00:14:46.950 --> 00:14:48.590
Let's go!

00:15:49.530 --> 00:15:52.500
The light of the future, shining bright!

00:15:54.090 --> 00:15:55.640
Cure Happy!

00:15:57.800 --> 00:15:59.660
Dazzling sun!

00:15:59.660 --> 00:16:01.590
Hot-blooded power!

00:16:02.580 --> 00:16:04.220
Cure Sunny!

00:16:06.460 --> 00:16:09.580
Rock, paper, scissors! Sparkling bright...

00:16:10.910 --> 00:16:12.590
Cure Peace!

00:16:14.240 --> 00:16:17.680
Laying down the gauntlet, with courage blazing!

00:16:18.950 --> 00:16:20.800
Cure March!

00:16:23.090 --> 00:16:26.670
A gentle heart as pure as the driven snow...

00:16:27.890 --> 00:16:29.490
Cure Beauty!

00:16:31.340 --> 00:16:33.720
Our five lights will blaze a path to the future!

00:16:39.990 --> 00:16:44.230
Shining bright, Smile Precure!

00:16:46.860 --> 00:16:50.400
Precure! I won't let you get between me and my meal!

00:16:50.670 --> 00:16:53.800
Come forth, Akanbe!

00:16:55.900 --> 00:16:58.370
Akanbe!

00:17:03.940 --> 00:17:05.870
Akakakakaka!

00:17:07.920 --> 00:17:11.290
That's not how you're supposed to use sauce! {RL: Really? CLEARLY you've never been to pixiv}

00:17:11.290 --> 00:17:14.550
The heck?! This is glue, not sauce!

00:17:14.550 --> 00:17:15.960
Be careful, everyone!

00:17:15.960 --> 00:17:17.660
Akanbe!

00:17:22.890 --> 00:17:23.870
March!

00:17:24.910 --> 00:17:26.700
Now's my chance...{TLC: sug. "Now's my chance..." here...}

00:17:31.010 --> 00:17:33.650
Time to eat!{TLC: ...and "...to dig in!", here}

00:17:35.350 --> 00:17:36.950
That's my okonomiyaki!

00:17:43.990 --> 00:17:45.920
Look... it's getting stronger!

00:17:45.920 --> 00:17:49.210
It must be because Wolfrun ate all that okonomiyaki-kuru!{TLC: never question the logic in magical girl anime.  Just don't.}

00:17:49.210 --> 00:17:50.090
Seriously?!

00:17:50.480 --> 00:17:54.630
Man, that hit the spot! Get them, Akanbe!

00:17:54.630 --> 00:17:56.600
Akanbe!

00:17:58.570 --> 00:17:59.470
Are you all okay?!

00:18:00.070 --> 00:18:01.300
I can't get free!

00:18:01.300 --> 00:18:02.610
Akanbe!

00:18:05.480 --> 00:18:06.810
Beauty!

00:18:07.710 --> 00:18:10.730
This human food of yours isn't half bad!

00:18:10.730 --> 00:18:12.300
Hey, thanks!

00:18:12.300 --> 00:18:13.820
Wait... who cares what you think!

00:18:14.430 --> 00:18:16.520
What are you thanking me for?

00:18:16.520 --> 00:18:19.220
'Cause I'm the one who made it!

00:18:20.320 --> 00:18:23.280
And... I'm meant to care? It's not like it matters who made it.

00:18:23.280 --> 00:18:29.330
Yeah, it does! No matter what I do, it's never gonna be as good as my dad's!

00:18:29.330 --> 00:18:33.040
You actually worry about this stuff? How pathetic!

00:18:33.040 --> 00:18:34.500
Pathetic?!

00:18:34.500 --> 00:18:37.340
How dare you! Akane-chan put everything she's got into making them!

00:18:37.340 --> 00:18:40.220
Who exactly is meant to care about that effort?

00:18:40.220 --> 00:18:42.810
Once it goes down the hatch, it's all the same.

00:18:42.810 --> 00:18:45.420
Besides, aren't these your failures?

00:18:45.770 --> 00:18:48.380
You've got some nerve!

00:18:48.380 --> 00:18:51.230
They aren't failures at all!

00:18:51.230 --> 00:18:52.910
I'm sure they were delicious!{TLC: "I bet they were delicious" "I'm sure they were delicious" "Of course they were delicious" seems more natural}

00:18:52.910 --> 00:18:58.430
Akane-chan put her heart and soul into making those!

00:19:01.470 --> 00:19:04.800
<i>What have I been teachin' you all this time for?</i>

00:19:05.040 --> 00:19:07.400
<i>True, it was burnt.</i>

00:19:08.370 --> 00:19:12.210
<i>But to your mother, it was the best meal I could have asked for.</i>

00:19:14.270 --> 00:19:15.760
So that's it...

00:19:16.260 --> 00:19:17.890
I get it...

00:19:17.890 --> 00:19:19.480
I get it!

00:19:19.480 --> 00:19:23.690
I've figured out my dad's secret ingredient!

00:19:25.330 --> 00:19:27.940
It's wantin' the person who eats it to enjoy it!{TLC: =_= I think I've watched too many of these shows.  As soon as the secret ingredient theme came up, I knew it had to be this. (It's only two seasons back since I last worked on an anime ep with this premise.)}

00:19:27.940 --> 00:19:30.160
And making sure that love fills every last bite...

00:19:30.570 --> 00:19:32.350
That's what my dad does...

00:19:32.350 --> 00:19:35.130
That's the secret of the Akane Okonomiyaki!

00:19:35.130 --> 00:19:39.300
Monologue time again, huh. Akanbe! Finish them already!

00:19:40.480 --> 00:19:43.230
Beauty! Shoot a Beauty Blizzard my way!

00:19:43.230 --> 00:19:44.710
What?! At <i>you</i>...?{TLC: not clear that she's asking why she'd shoot at Akane. "What?! At *you*?"}

00:19:44.820 --> 00:19:46.010
Just do it!

00:19:46.250 --> 00:19:47.610
As you wish!

00:19:49.110 --> 00:19:50.500
Precure...

00:19:53.020 --> 00:19:56.590
Beauty Blizzard!

00:19:58.300 --> 00:20:00.120
Alright!

00:20:07.560 --> 00:20:08.530
What?!

00:20:08.530 --> 00:20:09.500
Whoa!

00:20:16.370 --> 00:20:17.490
Akanbe!

00:20:28.680 --> 00:20:30.820
Akanbe!

00:20:34.370 --> 00:20:35.630
Precure...

00:20:35.630 --> 00:20:38.830
Sunny Fire!

00:20:44.070 --> 00:20:46.520
Akanbe...

00:20:53.140 --> 00:20:55.080
Hooray!

00:20:55.080 --> 00:20:57.550
It's the Umbrella Décor-kuru!

00:20:57.550 --> 00:21:00.650
That makes our tenth Décor-kuru!

00:21:02.020 --> 00:21:04.100
Damn you, Precure!

00:21:08.190 --> 00:21:09.680
Sorry for the wait!{TLC: *shrug*. In this situation, I normally go the liberal route with an "It's ready!", "Here's your order", etc, sort of line. Japanese waiting staff *always* say "I made you wait" in exactly the same situations English staff say "Here it is!".  A sincere remark about lateness is usually more like 「大変お待たせ」or whatever (something other than the standard service phrases).  I don't think it's any different from translating おはよう as "good morning" instead of "it's early"}{editor: Nah, it's fine the way it is}

00:21:09.680 --> 00:21:12.130
Thank you very much, dear.

00:21:16.220 --> 00:21:17.830
This is...

00:21:18.500 --> 00:21:20.070
...quite delicious!

00:21:20.090 --> 00:21:22.470
It just fills me with energy!

00:21:22.470 --> 00:21:25.680
You're your father's daughter, Akane-chan! This is fine cuisine!

00:21:25.680 --> 00:21:26.940
Alright, Akane-chan!

00:21:27.250 --> 00:21:29.710
Looks like you met his approval.

00:21:30.170 --> 00:21:32.750
I'm back from the hospital!

00:21:32.750 --> 00:21:34.220
Hino!

00:21:34.220 --> 00:21:36.850
This is some delicious okonomiyaki you serve here!

00:21:36.850 --> 00:21:38.690
Really? That's quite the honor!

00:21:39.500 --> 00:21:42.360
See? They all love your cooking!

00:21:43.130 --> 00:21:45.740
Well, I am your poster-girl, after all!

00:21:45.740 --> 00:21:48.430
Figuring out your secret ingredient was a piece of cake!{wasn't that difficult!}{TLC: sug. "was a piece of cake!" for nuance}{Meh, don't mind the original but I guess I'll let the qcers decide}

00:21:48.430 --> 00:21:50.420
You did, did you? Tell me what it is, then!

00:21:50.420 --> 00:21:52.560
Well...

00:21:53.390 --> 00:21:55.650
That's a secret!

00:21:57.050 --> 00:21:59.040
How is it a secret?!

00:21:59.040 --> 00:22:00.860
Payback for before!

00:23:39.440 --> 00:23:40.410
What is that huge thing?!

00:23:40.640 --> 00:23:42.640
It's a big hairy monster!

00:23:42.640 --> 00:23:44.010
Wait, is that Candy?!

00:23:44.010 --> 00:23:47.560
Where've you all gone-kuru?

00:23:47.560 --> 00:23:50.740
No, it's us! We've shrunk!

00:23:50.740 --> 00:23:52.840
We really have! Look at that huge grasshopper!{TAKA, TORA, BATTA! TA-TO-BA, TATOBA TA TO BA}{<-Mag left that note I'm guessing, kinda obvious :P}

00:23:52.840 --> 00:23:54.690
Look at those giant woodlice, too!

00:23:54.960 --> 00:23:56.700
Eww, giant bugs!

00:23:56.700 --> 00:23:58.690
Nao, snap out of it!

00:23:58.690 --> 00:24:00.000
Smile Precure.

00:24:02.260 --> 00:24:04.470
Find your ultra happy smile!
